  "notes": "Source: 'Program: Computer Science BS' recommended curriculum tables, official 2021-2022 Undergraduate and Graduate Catalog [ARCHIVED CATALOG], Texas Tech University, retrieved 2026-09-30 from https://catalog.ttu.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=15&poid=11087. Catalog year: 2021-2022 — this is an ARCHIVED official catalog, not the current 2025-2026 catalog. The current catalog's base 'Computer Science BS' program page could not be retrieved (the catalog's degree-plan index returned HTTP 403 and the base program page is not discoverable via public search; only the 2025-2026 concentration pages for Software Engineering and Cybersecurity were reachable). Transcription method: manual, course-by-course transcription of the catalog's 'Recommended Foundational Curriculum for Engineering All Majors — First Year' table and the 'Recommended Curriculum' tables for Second, Third, and Fourth Year; every course code, title, and credit value is verbatim from the tables, and per-semester sums were recomputed and verified against the catalog's stated semester totals and the stated 'Total Hours: 126' (verified sum 126). IMPORTANT CAVEATS: (1) The CS curriculum has changed since 2021-2022 — Texas Tech's official CS department 2025-2026 curriculum flowchart shows a new first-year engineering course (ENGR 1340) and three undergraduate concentrations (Software Engineering, Cybersecurity, and a third) beginning Fall 2025, so current students must confirm their plan against their entry-year catalog and an advisor. (2) Per-course prerequisites are NOT stated in the curriculum tables, so no prereq values are asserted (all prereq arrays are empty) — prerequisites appear in the catalog's course descriptions. (3) The catalog's 'Foreign Language/Spanish: 0 to 10 hours' requirement is not part of the 126-hour table. (4) The 3-hour Multicultural Requirement is recommended to double-count with the Creative Arts or Social & Behavioral Sciences core requirement, so it does not add hours beyond the table. (5) The 'Optional MATH minor' line in Third Year Spring is informational, not a course, and is not included as a course. (6) Communication Literacy for the CS program is met through CS 1382, CS 1412, CS 3365, and CS 4366 per the catalog. (7) Fourth Year Spring lists 'Elective (CS) 6 Semester Credit Hours' as a single line; it is transcribed as one 6-credit choice slot representing two 3-credit CS electives. CS elective footnote: choose from any 3000- or 4000-level computer science courses not required for the CS major.",
